cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "Please cite this repository when using its experimental evidence, verification artefacts, results, or supporting documentation. The repository-level metadata describes the research evidence repository as a whole; the frozen v1.0.0 and v1.1.0 evidence releases are identified below."

title: "ML-KEM CBMC Verification Case-Study Evidence"

type: dataset

authors:
  - given-names: "Girish"
    family-names: "Nallan Chakravathy"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Girish2052003/girish-nallan-chakravathy-thesis-2026-mlkem-cbmc-verification-case-study-evidences"

url: "https://github.com/Girish2052003/girish-nallan-chakravathy-thesis-2026-mlkem-cbmc-verification-case-study-evidences"

date-released: "2026-07-19"

abstract: "A versioned research evidence repository supporting an MSc thesis case study on AI-assisted formal verification of selected ML-KEM implementation components with CBMC. The repository preserves property-verification harnesses, assumptions, CBMC commands and outputs, mutation and negative-control results, source-revision records, manifests, checksums, reports, provenance records, and supporting scientific documentation. The V5 case-study evidence baseline is frozen in release v1.0.0, while release v1.1.0 preserves that baseline and adds the V1-V4 architectural-development evidence supporting RQ2."

keywords:
  - "ML-KEM"
  - "CBMC"
  - "formal verification"
  - "post-quantum cryptography"
  - "C verification"
  - "verification evidence"
  - "bounded model checking"
  - "research reproducibility"

